   local="Rishikesh stretches along both banks of the Ganga where the river leaves the hills. The town centre and Triveni Ghat sit on the flat ground, while Muni Ki Reti, Tapovan and the Laxman Jhula side climb into the hills on narrow roads and steep lanes. AIIMS Rishikesh, on the Virbhadra side near the old IDPL township, employs thousands of doctors, nurses and staff, and yoga schools and ashrams bring in long-stay residents from India and abroad. The town is also the gateway to the Char Dham road, so the highway is busy with yatra traffic from late April, and the Kanwar Yatra in Sawan brings huge crowds headed for Neelkanth.",
   areas=["Triveni Ghat area","Rishikesh town","Muni Ki Reti","Tapovan","Laxman Jhula side","Swarg Ashram","AIIMS and Virbhadra side","IDPL township","Shyampur","Raiwala","Dhalwala","Gumaniwala","Shivpuri"],
   routes=["Rishikesh to Delhi","Rishikesh to Chandigarh","Rishikesh to Gurugram","Rishikesh to Noida","Rishikesh to Jaipur","Rishikesh to Bengaluru"],
