   local="Roorkee is built along the Upper Ganga Canal, which runs straight through the town, and around one of India's oldest engineering institutions, IIT Roorkee, which began as the Thomason College. The Roorkee Cantonment is home to the Bengal Engineer Group, the Bengal Sappers, and national institutes such as the Central Building Research Institute and the National Institute of Hydrology add scientists and staff. Professors and officers live in campus and cantonment quarters, while families and students rent in Civil Lines, Ramnagar, Ganeshpur and the Awas Vikas colonies. To the west, the Bhagwanpur industrial area has factories whose staff live in Roorkee. The town sits on the Delhi to Haridwar highway, so the Kanwar Yatra in Sawan has a big effect on traffic.",
   areas=["Civil Lines","Ramnagar","Ganeshpur","Awas Vikas","Solani Puram","Adarsh Nagar","IIT campus side","Roorkee Cantonment","Salempur","Dhandera","Bhagwanpur","Manglaur"],
